// ListK8sVersions List offered Kubernetes versions
//
// The Kubernetes versions a cluster can currently be created on or
// upgraded to. **Public — no authentication required**, so the pre-login
// portal wizard can populate its picker. Subject to the global rate limit.
//
// This endpoint is the authoritative source for that picker: a version
// absent from this list is rejected by cluster creation and by upgrade
// with `422`.
//
// Each `version` is a **minor** (`"1.37"`), not a full patch version.
// Create and upgrade accept either form — a bare minor resolves to the
// latest patch Aether has verified for it, and a full
// `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` is accepted when its minor is offered and the patch
// is one this platform has resolved (at or below the minor's current
// `patch`); otherwise `422`.
//
// Every entry also carries `patch`: the full version that minor currently
// resolves to (`"1.37.0"`), so a picker can show the concrete version
// alongside the label without a second call.
//
// The list is every Kubernetes minor upstream still supports that the
// deployed Talos worker image can run, ordered newest-first. Two bounds,
// not three:
//
//   - **Upstream's support window** — the minors whose `endOfLifeDate` in
//     the Kubernetes release schedule has not passed. Normally three;
//     **four** during the ~2-month overlap after a new minor ships. Do not
//     assume a maximum of three entries.
//   - **The deployed Talos worker image** (`AETHER_TALOS_VERSION`) caps the
//     top. A minor the worker OS cannot run is never offered: the tenant
//     control plane would roll to a version no kubelet can match. Every
//     patch of an offered minor is runnable by that image, so the cap never
//     refuses a patch of a minor this endpoint lists.
//
// aether-operator accepts the uncapped upstream window, so everything
// offered here is provisionable by construction — both components read
// the same resolver (`github.com/plane-shift/k8s-versions-go`) rather
// than each deriving a window of its own.
//
// A minor upstream supports but for which no patch release has been
// published yet is not offered (there is nothing to deploy), though the
// operator would accept it.
//
// When the list is non-empty, exactly one entry is labelled `Latest` —
// the topmost minor that survives the Talos cap, which is **not**
// necessarily upstream's latest. Every other entry is labelled `Stable`.
//
// A Talos update never changes a tenant's Kubernetes version (owner ruling
// 2026-09-15); it only changes which versions this endpoint can offer.
// The list can therefore shrink underneath a running cluster, and that
// cluster keeps the version it is on.
