// ListRegions List regions
//
// The regions the platform knows about. `region` on cluster creation
// must name a region with an enabled Proxmox endpoint configured on this
// instance (otherwise `422` `validation_error`); the cluster is recorded
// under the region this API instance serves. `available` is
// informational. **Public — no authentication required**, so the
// pre-login signup wizard can populate its picker. Subject to the global
// rate limit.
//
// `available` is true only for the region this API instance itself
// serves (its `AETHER_REGION` setting); every other entry is
// informational and is **not** what cluster creation checks.
//
// Cluster creation accepts only a region this instance can place into:
// `POST /api/v1/organizations/{orgId}/clusters` resolves the requested
// `region` to an enabled Proxmox endpoint and rejects a region with none
// with `422` (`validation_error`, a message naming the region:
// `No Proxmox endpoint is configured for region eu-fi`). The created
// cluster is recorded under the region this instance serves.
//
// The list is static in the binary today — it is not read from the
// database and does not reflect capacity.
//
